
========
EASYMENU
========

SHORT DESCRIPTION
=================

Easymenu is a script used to generate a multi-level menu system.

BACKGROUND
==========

It is the year 2026. 25 years ago, I created Easymenu to solve some
of my every day work problems. Back then, it was publicly released
and had a little user base in the Linux and Unix community. Since
then, most places where you could find it, like Freshmeat, has died
and there are almost no records of Easymenu ever existing. But the
source code has been safely tucked away in my archives since the last
release, so I decided to re-relase it on GitHub. Mostly for the fun
of it, but who knows, perhaps this very mature piece of shell script
can be of use to someone in the future.

Enjoy!


INTRO 
=====

Easymenu can be used to generate anything from easy one-level menus
to advanced multi-level menusystems. It has a set of internal
commands, and can execute external applications and scripts, all
to be as flexible as possible.

Easymenu needs only one file to run, which makes it very easy to
install and remove from your system. Configuration files and menus
can be stored just about anywhere you like in the system, and can
easily be removed or backed up.

The goal of Easymenu is to provide a platform independent software
that is easy to install and configure, and doesn't require a compiler
or other tools.


